				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "Diodes Incorporated AP3036B, SOT-23-6, boost LED driver. Pin1=CTRL (EN/PWM dimming), pin2=VOUT, pin3=VIN, pin4=SW, pin5=GND, pin6=FB -- per Diodes' own AP3036B datasheet (DS37004 Rev 2-2). Used here as the backlight driver for the CFAF240320A0-024SN display's LED_A/LED_K string, exactly matching Crystalfontz's own 'LED Backlight Reference Schematic' (datasheet section 11.2): L1 22uH 1210 (VIN to SW), C16 10uF 0805 (VIN bypass), C17 1uF 0805 (VOUT to GND), R6 5.1 ohm 0402 (FB to GND, sets ILED ~=39.2mA). LCSC C526368 -- re-checked live via jlcpcb-search MCP on 2026-11-15: still 0 units in stock (same as the bead's investigation comment). The bead-named fallback AW9364DNR (LCSC C401007) was independently verified against its own datasheet and rejected: it is a 4-channel linear constant-current LED *sink* (VIN 2.8-5.5V, 20mA/channel, no inductor), not a boost converter, and cannot produce this backlight's required ~9V/40mA string voltage -- using it would not work, not just differ in pinout. AP3036BKTR-G1 is kept here as the only circuit that is actually correct for this backlight; the 0-stock status is a BOM/sourcing risk flagged for pilink-7el.8, not a schematic defect."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
